  ('secret-stripe-live', 'generic', 'Exposed secret', 'critical',
   'Live Stripe secret key exposed in client bundle',
   'A Stripe live secret key (sk_live_*) was found in JavaScript or HTML served to the browser, and a harmless read against Stripe''s Balance API confirmed the key is active. AI payment scaffolds routinely ship Stripe server keys via NEXT_PUBLIC_* or VITE_* env vars.',
   'A live Stripe secret key allows charges, refunds and reading customer data.',
   'rule_ref',
   '{"rule":"stripeLiveKeyProbe"}'::jsonb,
   'free',
   '{"summary":"Rotate the Stripe secret key now and move it server-side.","steps":["Roll the secret key in the Stripe dashboard immediately.","Remove sk_live_* from all client code and client-exposed env vars (NEXT_PUBLIC_*, VITE_*).","Use Stripe publishable keys (pk_live_*) in the browser and keep secret keys in server routes only."]}'::jsonb,
   'A live Stripe secret key (sk_live_*) is exposed in my client bundle and validated as active. Remove it from all client-side code and client-exposed environment variables, move every Stripe server call into server-side code, and tell me exactly which files referenced it so I can rotate the key.',
   true),
  ('secret-stripe-restricted', 'generic', 'Exposed secret', 'high',
