   '{"regex":"eyJ[A-Za-z0-9_-]{10,}\\\\.[A-Za-z0-9_-]{20,}\\\\.[A-Za-z0-9_-]{20,}","validate":"service_role","secretName":"Supabase service_role JWT","serverOnly":true}'::jsonb,
   'free',
   '{"summary":"Rotate the Supabase service_role JWT now and move it server-side.","steps":["Treat the key as compromised and rotate it with the provider immediately.","Remove it from all client code and from any client-exposed env var (e.g. NEXT_PUBLIC_*, VITE_*).","Access the key only from server-side code (route handlers / serverless functions)."]}'::jsonb,
   'A Supabase service_role JWT is exposed in my client bundle. Remove it from all client-side code and client-exposed environment variables, move every use of it into server-side code, and tell me exactly which files referenced it so I can rotate and confirm.',
   true),
  ('secret-twilio', 'generic', 'Exposed secret', 'high',
   'Twilio account SID + auth token exposed in client bundle',
   'A Twilio account SID paired with its auth token was found in JavaScript or HTML served to the browser.',
   'Twilio credentials can be abused to send SMS/calls on your bill.',
   'rule_ref',
   '{"rule":"twilioCredentialsInClient"}'::jsonb,
   'free',
   '{"summary":"Rotate the Twilio auth token now and move credentials server-side.","steps":["Rotate the Twilio auth token in the Twilio console immediately.","Remove accountSid and authToken from all client code and client-exposed env vars.","Proxy SMS/OTP sends through a server route that holds the credentials."]}'::jsonb,
   'My Twilio account SID and auth token are exposed in the client bundle. Move all Twilio API calls to server-side code, remove TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN from any NEXT_PUBLIC_/VITE_ env vars, and show me exactly which files referenced the credentials so I can rotate the auth token.',
   true),
  ('server-side-eval-evidence', 'generic', 'Injection', 'critical',
   'Server handler passes request body to eval()',
   'Application source (bundled or tutorial-visible) shows eval(req.body.*) or eval(req.query.*) — a classic server-side JavaScript injection pattern in Node/Express apps.',
   'User input is passed to eval() on the server — remote code execution is likely.',
   'rule_ref',
   '{"rule":"serverSideEvalEvidence"}'::jsonb,
   'deep',
   '{"summary":"Remove eval(); parse input with JSON.parse or typed parsers.","steps":["Delete eval() and new Function() calls that read req.body or req.query.","Use JSON.parse with schema validation for structured input.","Return generic errors; never execute user strings as code."]}'::jsonb,
   'My Node/Express handler uses eval(req.body.field) to parse user input. Remove eval(), parse with JSON.parse + validation, and show the safe handler.',
   true),
  ('client-side-ctf-platform-evidence', 'generic', 'Broken access control', 'medium',
   'CTF challenge platform SPA with public challenge APIs',
   'The shipped JavaScript documents a Hackforge-style CTF platform with publicChallenges(), flag submission UI, and admin challenge routes — challenge metadata and APIs are exposed in the client bundle.',
   'Public CTF platform bundle reveals challenge APIs and flag workflows attackers can enumerate.',
   'rule_ref',
   '{"rule":"clientSideCtfPlatformEvidence"}'::jsonb,
   'deep',
   '{"summary":"Gate challenge APIs behind auth; avoid shipping admin routes in public bundles.","steps":["Require login before listing or fetching challenge details.","Move admin challenge management off the public SPA bundle.","Rate-limit flag submission endpoints server-side."]}'::jsonb,
   'Our CTF platform SPA ships publicChallenges APIs and CTF{ flag submission UI in the client bundle. Show how to gate challenge routes behind authenticated APIs and remove admin paths from the production bundle.',
   true),
  ('spring-boot-actuator-exposed', 'generic', 'Security misconfiguration', 'high',
   'Spring Boot actuator endpoints exposed',
   'Spring Boot management endpoints (/actuator) respond with JSON to unauthenticated requests. Attackers can read health, git commit info, and sometimes environment secrets depending on exposure settings.',
   'Management/monitoring endpoints are publicly reachable — config and secrets may leak.',
   'rule_ref',
   '{"rule":"springActuatorExposed"}'::jsonb,
   'free',
   '{"summary":"Restrict actuator to internal networks and disable sensitive endpoints in production.","steps":["Set management.endpoints.web.exposure.include to only what you need (often just health).","Require authentication on /actuator or move it off the public internet.","Disable env, heapdump, and configprops endpoints in production."]}'::jsonb,
   'My Spring Boot app exposes /actuator publicly (health/info/_links JSON). Lock down management endpoints: restrict exposure, require auth, and show me the application.properties / application.yml changes.',
   true),
  ('sql-error-disclosure', 'generic', 'Injection', 'high',
   'SQL syntax error disclosed on search/query input',
   'A search or filter endpoint returns a raw database syntax error when given malformed input, proving the parameter is interpolated into SQL. This is positive proof of SQL injection risk.',
   'Attackers can read or modify your database via the search parameter.',
   'rule_ref',
   '{"rule":"sqlErrorDisclosure"}'::jsonb,
   'deep',
   '{"summary":"Use parameterized queries; never concatenate user input into SQL.","steps":["Replace string-concatenated queries with prepared statements / ORM bindings.","Return generic errors to clients; log SQL details server-side only.","Add input validation and WAF rules on search endpoints."]}'::jsonb,
   'My search endpoint returns SQL syntax errors (e.g. SQLITE_ERROR) when given malformed input. Switch to parameterized queries/ORM bindings, return generic errors to clients, and show me the fixed handler.',
   true),
  ('stack-cors-wildcard-api', 'generic', 'Misconfiguration', 'high',
   'API reflects Access-Control-Allow-Origin: * with credentials path',
   'AI-generated APIs often set CORS to * so demos work, which enables any site to call your API from a victim''s browser.',
   'Any website can call your API from users'' browsers.',
   'rule_ref',
   '{"rule":"permissiveCors"}'::jsonb,
   'deep',
   '{"summary":"Restrict CORS to your real front-end origins.","steps":["Set Access-Control-Allow-Origin to explicit origins.","Avoid * when cookies or auth headers are used."]}'::jsonb,
   'My API uses Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *. Restrict CORS to my real front-end origins and show the updated server config.',
   true),
  ('stack-database-url-in-bundle', 'generic', 'Exposed secret', 'critical',
   'Database connection string in client bundle',
   'Postgres/Neon/Prisma DATABASE_URL (or similar) appears in JavaScript served to the browser. AI scaffolds often import server config into shared modules.',
   'Anyone can connect to your database with the credentials in the page source.',
   'secret_regex',
   '{"_raw":"{ regex: \"(?:postgres(?:ql)?|mysql):\\\\/\\\\/[^\\\\s\\\"'']{12,}\", secretName: \"Database connection URL\", serverOnly: true }"}'::jsonb,
   'free',
   '{"summary":"Remove the connection string from all client code and rotate DB credentials.","steps":["Keep DATABASE_URL only in server env.","Rotate the database password.","Use a server-only data access layer."]}'::jsonb,
   'A database connection string is in my client bundle. Remove every client reference, keep DATABASE_URL server-only, and tell me to rotate the database password.',
   true),
  ('stack-neon-url-in-bundle', 'generic', 'Exposed secret', 'critical',
   'Neon / serverless Postgres URL in client',
   'Neon connection strings in client JS give full database access. Common when AI copies .env into a shared config module.',
   'Your Neon database credentials are public.',
   'secret_regex',
   '{"regex":"ep-[a-z0-9-]+\\.[a-z0-9.-]+\\.neon\\.tech","secretName":"Neon host","serverOnly":true}'::jsonb,
   'free',
   '{"summary":"Keep Neon credentials server-side and rotate.","steps":["Remove Neon URLs from client bundles.","Rotate the role password in Neon."]}'::jsonb,
   'A Neon database host/credential appears in my client bundle. Move all DB access server-side and rotate the Neon role password.',
   true),
  ('stack-vercel-env-exposure', 'generic', 'Source exposure', 'medium',
   'Vercel / Next build manifest or env debug endpoint',
   'Debug or build artifacts sometimes remain reachable on Vercel deploys from AI templates.',
   'Build or env debug surfaces may leak configuration.',
   'http_probe',
   '{"paths":["/_next/static/chunks/env.js","/api/debug","/api/env","/.vercel/project.json"],"expect":{"kind":"status_2xx_non_html"},"maxBytes":4096}'::jsonb,
   'deep',
   '{"summary":"Remove debug routes and never deploy env dumps.","steps":["Delete debug API routes.","Confirm they 404 in production."]}'::jsonb,
   'My Vercel/Next deploy may expose debug or env endpoints. Remove them and confirm they return 404 in production.',
   true),
  ('supabase-anon-key-no-rls', 'supabase', 'Broken access control', 'high',
   'Supabase anon key exposed with Row Level Security disabled',
   'Exposing the anon key client-side is expected and safe ONLY when Row Level Security protects every table. AI builders frequently create tables without enabling RLS, so the anon key alone can read or write data.',
   'Visitors may be able to read or modify your data directly, with no login.',
   'rule_ref',
   '{"rule":"supabaseRls","options":{"harmlessProbe":true}}'::jsonb,
   'free',
   '{"summary":"Enable Row Level Security on every table and add owner-scoped policies.","steps":["In Supabase, enable RLS on each table under Authentication > Policies.","Add policies that restrict rows to the authenticated owner (e.g. user_id = auth.uid()).","Re-test by querying with the anon key while signed out."]}'::jsonb,
   'Some of my Supabase tables have Row Level Security disabled, so the public anon key can read/write them. Enable RLS on every table and generate owner-scoped policies (rows visible only to the authenticated owner). Output the SQL for each policy.',
   true),
  ('supabase-service-role-in-bundle', 'supabase', 'Exposed secret', 'critical',
   'Supabase service_role key shipped to the browser',
   'The Supabase service_role key bypasses Row Level Security entirely. AI builders sometimes wire it into client code or an exposed env var because they put .env access on the client by default. Anyone can read and write every row in your database.',
   'Full read/write access to your entire database for anyone who views your site source.',
   'secret_regex',
   '{"_raw":"{ // service_role JWTs are standard JWTs whose payload contains \"role\":\"service_role\". regex: \"eyJ[A-Za-z0-9_-]{10,}\\\\.[A-Za-z0-9_-]{20,}\\\\.[A-Za-z0-9_-]{20,}\", validate: \"service_role\", secretName: \"Supabase service_role key\", serverOnly: true }"}'::jsonb,
   'free',
   '{"summary":"Remove the service_role key from all client code and rotate it immediately.","steps":["Rotate the service_role key in Supabase > Project Settings > API.","Delete any client-side usage; only use it in server-side code (route handlers / Edge functions).","Use the anon key on the client and rely on Row Level Security for access control."]}'::jsonb,
   'My Supabase service_role key is exposed in the client bundle. Remove every client-side use of the service_role key, switch the browser client to the anon key, and move any privileged database access into server-side route handlers. Then list every place the service_role key was referenced so I can confirm it is gone.',
   true),
  ('tech-stack-disclosure', 'generic', 'Information disclosure', 'low',
   'Server/framework version disclosed in headers',
   'Response headers (Server, X-Powered-By, X-AspNet-Version) reveal the exact software and version running, which lets an attacker look up known CVEs for that version directly.',
   'Headers reveal your exact stack/version, guiding targeted exploits.',
   'rule_ref',
   '{"rule":"techDisclosure"}'::jsonb,
   'free',
   '{"_raw":"{ summary: \"Suppress version-revealing response headers.\", steps: [ \"Remove or blank the X-Powered-By header (e.g. app.disable(''x-powered-by'')).\", \"Strip version numbers from the Server header at your proxy/CDN.\", \"Remove X-AspNet-Version / framework version headers.\" ] }"}'::jsonb,
   'My site leaks its stack via Server / X-Powered-By / X-AspNet-Version headers. Remove or anonymise these version-disclosing response headers in my framework and proxy config, and show me how.',
   true),
  ('unauthenticated-admin-endpoint', 'generic', 'Broken authentication', 'critical',
   'Admin or application configuration reachable without authentication',
   'An administrative configuration endpoint responds with application settings to unauthenticated GET requests. Attackers gain internal config, feature flags, and sometimes secrets.',
   'Anyone can read your admin/application configuration over HTTP.',
   'rule_ref',
   '{"rule":"unauthenticatedAdminEndpoint"}'::jsonb,
   'free',
   '{"summary":"Require admin authentication on every configuration endpoint.","steps":["Gate /admin and /rest/admin routes behind session + role checks.","Return 401/403 for unauthenticated callers.","Never expose full application config in production APIs."]}'::jsonb,
   'My /rest/admin/application-configuration (or similar admin config route) returns JSON without authentication. Add admin session + role checks and return 401 for unauthenticated requests. Show the middleware.',
   true),
  ('unprotected-webhook-endpoint', 'generic', 'Broken authentication', 'high',
   'Payment webhook endpoint without signature verification',
   'A Stripe/Razorpay-style webhook path is reachable and appears to accept requests without verifying the provider signature. AI scaffolding very commonly omits signature verification, letting an attacker forge ''payment succeeded'' events.',
   'Attackers may forge payment events (e.g. fake ''paid'') if your webhook is unverified.',
   'rule_ref',
   '{"rule":"webhookSignature"}'::jsonb,
   'deep',
   '{"summary":"Verify the provider signature on every webhook before trusting it.","steps":["Read the raw request body and verify the provider signature header.","Reject any request whose signature does not validate.","Never grant entitlements before signature verification passes."]}'::jsonb,
   'My payment webhook endpoint may not verify the provider signature. Add strict signature verification (Stripe/Razorpay) using the raw request body before any business logic runs, and reject invalid signatures. Show me the handler.',
   true),
  ('v0-openapi-routes-exposed', 'v0', 'Information disclosure', 'medium',
   'v0 Next.js app exposes API schema docs',
   'v0-generated Next.js APIs often leave OpenAPI/Swagger routes from the template enabled, documenting every Server Action and route handler.',
   'Generated API docs reveal all v0 routes to attackers.',
   'rule_ref',
   '{"rule":"openApiDocs"}'::jsonb,
   'free',
   '{"summary":"Remove or protect API doc routes in production.","steps":["Delete or auth-gate /openapi.json and /docs.","Verify 404 in production."]}'::jsonb,
   'My v0 Next.js app exposes OpenAPI docs in production. Remove or protect those routes and confirm they 404 on the live deploy.',
   true),
  ('v0-server-action-no-authz', 'v0', 'Broken access control', 'high',
   'Next.js Server Action without authorization check',
   'v0-generated Next.js apps often expose Server Actions that mutate data without re-checking the caller''s identity/permissions, trusting the UI to gate access.',
   'A generated Server Action may let any caller perform privileged mutations.',
   'rule_ref',
   '{"rule":"serverActionAuthz"}'::jsonb,
   'deep',
   '{"summary":"Authorize inside every Server Action.","steps":["Re-validate the session and permissions at the top of each Server Action.","Never rely on the calling component being hidden."]}'::jsonb,
   'My Next.js Server Actions mutate data without checking who is calling them. Add session + permission checks at the start of each Server Action and reject unauthorized callers. Show the updated actions.',
   true),
  ('verbose-error-disclosure', 'generic', 'Information disclosure', 'medium',
   'Verbose error / stack trace exposed in production',
   'A malformed request triggers a full framework stack trace or debug error page in production, leaking file paths, dependency versions, and sometimes secrets. Debug mode is frequently left on in AI-scaffolded deploys.',
   'Error pages leak your file paths, stack, and versions to attackers.',
   'rule_ref',
   '{"rule":"errorDisclosure"}'::jsonb,
   'deep',
   '{"_raw":"{ summary: \"Disable debug mode in production and return generic error pages.\", steps: [ \"Set the framework to production mode (debug off) so stack traces aren''t rendered.\", \"Return generic 4xx/5xx pages without internal details.\", \"Log full errors server-side only, never in the HTTP response.\" ] }"}'::jsonb,
   'My production app returns verbose stack traces / debug error pages on bad input. Turn off debug mode in production, return generic error pages, and keep detailed errors in server logs only. Show me the config.',
   true),
  ('vibe-algolia-admin-in-client', 'generic', 'Exposed secret', 'critical',
   'Algolia admin API key in client bundle',
   'Algolia''s admin API key grants full index control (create, delete, settings, browse all records). AI search integrations often copy the admin key into NEXT_PUBLIC_ or VITE_ env vars instead of the restricted search-only key.',
   'Your Algolia admin key in JS lets anyone rewrite indexes and exfiltrate all search data.',
   'rule_ref',
   '{"rule":"algoliaAdminKeyInClient"}'::jsonb,
   'free',
   '{"summary":"Use the search-only API key client-side and rotate the admin key.","steps":["Replace client-side admin keys with the Algolia search-only API key.","Keep admin operations (reindex, settings) in server routes or Edge Functions only.","Rotate the admin API key in the Algolia dashboard → API Keys."]}'::jsonb,
   'My client bundle exposes an Algolia admin API key (ALGOLIA_ADMIN_API_KEY or adminApiKey). Switch the browser to the search-only key, move admin/index operations server-side, and tell me to rotate the admin key.',
   true),
  ('vibe-auth0-secret-in-client', 'generic', 'Exposed secret', 'critical',
   'Auth0 client secret referenced in client bundle',
   'Auth0 quickstarts and NextAuth Auth0Provider configs often assign AUTH0_CLIENT_SECRET or clientSecret in modules that ship to the browser. Only the client ID belongs client-side; the secret enables token exchange and session forgery.',
   'Your Auth0 client secret in JS enables OAuth token theft and account takeover.',
   'rule_ref',
   '{"rule":"auth0SecretInClient"}'::jsonb,
   'free',
   '{"summary":"Move Auth0 secret usage server-side and rotate the client secret.","steps":["Remove AUTH0_CLIENT_SECRET from all client code and client-exposed env vars (NEXT_PUBLIC_*, VITE_*).","Handle Auth0 token exchange only in server routes or Edge Functions.","Rotate the client secret in Auth0 Dashboard → Applications → Settings."]}'::jsonb,
   'My frontend references an Auth0 client secret (AUTH0_CLIENT_SECRET or clientSecret). Move all Auth0 secret usage to server-side API routes, remove it from client-exposed env vars, and tell me to rotate the client secret in Auth0.',
   true),
  ('vibe-clerk-secret-in-client', 'generic', 'Exposed secret', 'critical',
   'Clerk secret key referenced in client bundle',
   'Clerk''s sk_live_ / sk_test_ secret is assigned in client-side code. Only the publishable key (pk_) belongs in the browser.',
   'Your Clerk secret key in JS grants full auth admin on your app.',
   'rule_ref',
   '{"rule":"clerkSecretInClient"}'::jsonb,
   'free',
   '{"summary":"Move Clerk secret operations server-side and rotate the key.","steps":["Use pk_ keys client-side only.","Use sk_ keys in API routes / Edge Functions only.","Rotate in Clerk dashboard."]}'::jsonb,
   'My frontend references a Clerk secret key (sk_live/sk_test). Move all Clerk secret usage to server-side API routes and tell me to rotate the key.',
   true),
  ('vibe-demo-auth-bypass-flag', 'generic', 'Broken access control', 'high',
   'Demo / skip-auth flag enabled in shipped bundle',
   'Vibe-coded apps frequently ship SKIP_AUTH, DEMO_MODE, or BYPASS_AUTH toggles left on from scaffolding. Anyone can flip the same flag in DevTools or read it from the bundle.',
   'A hard-coded auth bypass flag is live in your production JavaScript.',
   'rule_ref',
   '{"rule":"demoModeFlags"}'::jsonb,
   'free',
   '{"_raw":"{ summary: \"Remove demo auth bypass flags from production builds.\", steps: [ \"Delete SKIP_AUTH / DEMO_MODE / BYPASS_AUTH constants from client code.\", \"Gate any dev-only bypass behind NODE_ENV === ''development'' on the server only.\", \"Rotate sessions if the bypass was ever deployed publicly.\" ] }"}'::jsonb,
   'My app ships with SKIP_AUTH, DEMO_MODE, or BYPASS_AUTH enabled in the client bundle. Remove every auth bypass flag from production code and enforce auth server-side only.',
   true),
  ('vibe-exposed-admin-panel', 'generic', 'Broken access control', 'critical',
   'Admin panel reachable without authentication',
   'A common admin path (/admin, /dashboard, /manage) returns an admin UI with management tables or copy — without redirecting to a login page. AI scaffolds often ship admin dashboards as client-only routes with no server-side gate.',
   'Anyone can open your admin panel URL and use management features without signing in.',
   'rule_ref',
   '{"rule":"exposedAdminPanel"}'::jsonb,
   'free',
   '{"summary":"Protect every admin route with server-side authentication.","steps":["Add middleware or server layout checks that return 401/redirect for unauthenticated requests.","Never rely on client-side route guards alone for /admin or /dashboard.","Audit admin mutations to require a verified session on the server."]}'::jsonb,
   'My /admin or /dashboard route is reachable without authentication — visitors see the admin UI without logging in. Add server-side auth middleware on every admin route, redirect unauthenticated users to login, and show me the middleware/config changes.',
   true),
  ('vibe-firebase-firestore-open', 'firebase', 'Broken access control', 'high',
   'Firestore collection readable without authentication',
   'Firebase web config + open security rules let anyone with the API key list documents from common collections (users, profiles, posts).',
   'Firestore returns documents to unauthenticated callers.',
   'rule_ref',
   '{"rule":"firebaseFirestoreOpen"}'::jsonb,
   'free',
   '{"summary":"Tighten Firestore security rules to require auth.","steps":["Add request.auth != null checks.","Scope reads/writes to the owning user.","Audit exposed collections."]}'::jsonb,
   'My Firestore returns documents without authentication. Tighten security rules so reads require auth and users can only access their own data.',
   true),
  ('vibe-hardcoded-demo-credentials', 'generic', 'Broken authentication', 'high',
   'Hardcoded demo credentials in client bundle',
   'The shipped JavaScript contains literal admin/password or demo@test.com credentials from AI scaffolding — readable in DevTools.',
   'Default demo login credentials are embedded in your production JavaScript.',
   'rule_ref',
   '{"rule":"hardcodedCredentials"}'::jsonb,
   'free',
   '{"summary":"Remove all hardcoded credentials from client code.","steps":["Delete demo login constants.","Use server-side auth only.","Rotate any accounts that used demo passwords."]}'::jsonb,
   'My client bundle contains hardcoded demo credentials (admin/password or demo@test.com). Remove them from all client code and enforce auth server-side.',
   true),
  ('vibe-next-data-sensitive-keys', 'v0', 'Exposed secret', 'critical',
   'Sensitive env key names in Next.js __NEXT_DATA__',
   'Server secret key names (DATABASE_URL, SERVICE_ROLE, etc.) with values are serialized into __NEXT_DATA__ — visible in View Source on every page load.',
   'Secret configuration is embedded in the HTML payload shipped to every visitor.',
   'rule_ref',
   '{"rule":"nextDataSensitiveKeys"}'::jsonb,
   'free',
   '{"summary":"Never pass secrets through getServerSideProps/page props into __NEXT_DATA__.","steps":["Remove secret values from all page props.","Read secrets only in server route handlers.","Rotate anything that was exposed."]}'::jsonb,
   'My Next.js __NEXT_DATA__ contains sensitive env key names with values. Remove them from page props so they never reach the client, and list what I must rotate.',
   true),
  ('vibe-openapi-docs-exposed', 'generic', 'Information disclosure', 'medium',
   'OpenAPI / Swagger docs publicly reachable',
   'AI scaffolds often ship with /openapi.json or /swagger enabled in production. Attackers get a full map of every route, parameter, and mutation without guessing.',
   'Public API docs reveal every endpoint and schema to attackers.',
   'rule_ref',
   '{"rule":"openApiDocs"}'::jsonb,
   'free',
   '{"summary":"Disable or gate API documentation in production.","steps":["Remove or protect /openapi.json, /swagger, and /docs routes behind auth.","Use environment checks so docs only load in development.","Confirm production returns 404 for doc endpoints."]}'::jsonb,
   'My production app exposes OpenAPI/Swagger docs at paths like /openapi.json or /swagger. Disable or protect them behind auth in production and show the config changes.',
   true),
  ('vibe-public-cloud-storage-bucket', 'generic', 'Broken access control', 'critical',
   'Public cloud storage bucket lists objects without auth',
   'Your JavaScript references an S3, Google Cloud Storage, or Cloudflare R2 bucket URL, and a read-only list request returns real object names without credentials. AI upload scaffolds often hardcode bucket URLs and leave buckets world-readable.',
   'Anyone can list and download files from your cloud storage bucket.',
   'rule_ref',
   '{"rule":"publicCloudStorageBucket"}'::jsonb,
   'free',
   '{"summary":"Block public list/read on the bucket and use signed URLs for uploads.","steps":["Set the bucket to private and remove public ListBucket/GetObject permissions.","Use pre-signed URLs or a server-side upload proxy instead of public bucket URLs in the client.","Audit existing objects for sensitive uploads and rotate any exposed access keys."]}'::jsonb,
   'My app references a public S3/GCS/R2 bucket that lists objects without authentication. Make the bucket private, remove public list/read ACLs, switch uploads to signed URLs or a server proxy, and show the IAM/policy changes.',
   true),
  ('vibe-sitemap-sensitive-paths', 'generic', 'Information disclosure', 'medium',
   'sitemap.xml lists sensitive routes',
   'AI SEO scaffolds auto-generate sitemaps that include /admin, /api/internal, or /staging URLs — a crawlable map of your attack surface.',
   'Your sitemap advertises internal routes to search engines and attackers.',
   'rule_ref',
   '{"rule":"sitemapSensitivePaths"}'::jsonb,
   'free',
   '{"summary":"Remove sensitive URLs from sitemap.xml.","steps":["Exclude admin/internal paths from sitemap generation.","Protect those routes with auth."]}'::jsonb,
   'My sitemap.xml includes sensitive paths like /admin or /staging. Exclude them from sitemap generation and protect those routes with auth.',
   true),
  ('vibe-streamlit-secrets-exposed', 'generic', 'Source exposure', 'critical',
   'Streamlit secrets.toml reachable over HTTP',
   'Streamlit vibe apps deployed without proper static routing sometimes serve .streamlit/secrets.toml, leaking API keys and database passwords.',
   'Streamlit secrets file is downloadable from your public URL.',
   'http_probe',
   '{"paths":["/.streamlit/secrets.toml","/secrets.toml"],"expect":{"kind":"status_2xx_non_html"},"maxBytes":4096}'::jsonb,
   'free',
   '{"summary":"Block secrets.toml from the web root and rotate every leaked secret.","steps":["Configure the host to never serve .streamlit/ paths.","Rotate all keys that were in secrets.toml."]}'::jsonb,
   'My Streamlit deploy serves .streamlit/secrets.toml publicly. Block that path at the edge and tell me which secrets to rotate.',
   true),
  ('vibe-supabase-service-role-client', 'supabase', 'Exposed secret', 'critical',
   'Supabase service_role key wired into browser client',
   'AI builders pass the service_role JWT to createClient() in frontend code to ''make admin features work''. That key bypasses every RLS policy and grants full database access.',
   'The service_role key in your browser bundle bypasses all database security.',
   'rule_ref',
   '{"rule":"supabaseServiceRoleClient"}'::jsonb,
   'free',
   '{"summary":"Never use service_role in client code; rotate the key immediately.","steps":["Remove createClient(url, service_role_key) from all frontend files.","Move privileged operations to Edge Functions or server routes using service_role server-side only.","Rotate the service_role key in Supabase dashboard → Settings → API."]}'::jsonb,
   'My frontend calls createClient with the Supabase service_role key. Remove it from all client code, move admin operations to a server route or Edge Function, and tell me to rotate the service_role key.',
   true),
  ('vibe-supabase-storage-public', 'supabase', 'Broken access control', 'high',
   'Supabase Storage bucket marked public',
   'Lovable and Bolt scaffolds often create a ''public'' storage bucket with public:true. The anon key can list it and download any object unless you add RLS policies on storage.objects.',
   'A public Supabase bucket may expose uploads to anyone with the anon key.',
   'rule_ref',
   '{"rule":"supabaseStoragePublic"}'::jsonb,
   'free',
   '{"_raw":"{ summary: \"Make buckets private and add storage RLS policies.\", steps: [ \"Set public:false on buckets that hold user data.\", \"Add storage.objects policies restricting SELECT to authenticated users.\", \"Audit existing objects for sensitive uploads.\" ] }"}'::jsonb,
   'My Supabase project has a public storage bucket. Make buckets private, add storage RLS so only authenticated owners can read/write, and show the SQL policies.',
   true),
  ('vibe-unauthenticated-api-routes', 'generic', 'Broken access control', 'high',
   'JSON API routes return data without authentication',
   'Routes referenced in your client bundle respond with JSON to unauthenticated GET requests — a classic vibe-coded API with no session check on the server.',
   'API endpoints leak data to anyone who guesses or reads the path from your JS.',
   'rule_ref',
   '{"rule":"unauthenticatedApiRoutes"}'::jsonb,
   'deep',
   '{"summary":"Require authentication on every API route that returns user or business data.","steps":["Add session verification at the top of each handler.","Return 401 for missing/invalid auth.","Never rely on hiding routes in the UI."]}'::jsonb,
   'My API routes return JSON without checking authentication. Add session/auth verification to every sensitive route handler and return 401 when unauthenticated.',
   true),
  ('vibe-weak-csp', 'generic', 'Security misconfiguration', 'medium',
   'Content-Security-Policy allows unsafe-inline or unsafe-eval',
   'A CSP is present but includes unsafe-inline or unsafe-eval — the default AI template CSP that does not actually stop XSS.',
   'Your CSP still allows inline scripts, so XSS can bypass it.',
   'rule_ref',
   '{"rule":"weakCsp"}'::jsonb,
   'free',
   '{"summary":"Remove unsafe-inline and unsafe-eval from production CSP.","steps":["Use nonces or hashes for required inline scripts.","Drop unsafe-eval unless absolutely required."]}'::jsonb,
   'My CSP includes unsafe-inline or unsafe-eval. Tighten the Content-Security-Policy for production using nonces/hashes and remove unsafe directives.',
   true),
  ('windsurf-public-env-leak', 'windsurf', 'Exposed secret', 'high',
   'Public env prefix used for a privileged credential',
   'Windsurf-generated Vite/Next apps share the same public-prefix trap as Bolt and Cursor scaffolds.',
   'A privileged credential may be embedded in client JS.',
   'rule_ref',
   '{"rule":"publicEnvPrefixLeak"}'::jsonb,
   'free',
   '{"summary":"Keep privileged credentials server-side only.","steps":["Audit VITE_/NEXT_PUBLIC_ usage.","Rotate any leaked credential."]}'::jsonb,
   'My Windsurf-built app may expose secrets via public env prefixes. Find them, move them server-side, and list rotations needed.',
   true),
  ('client-side-prompt-injection-evidence', 'generic', 'AI security', 'medium',
   'Prompt-injection red-team or scanner functionality in client bundle',
   'The shipped JavaScript or SSR HTML documents prompt-injection attack tooling — adversarial prompt scanners, AI defender challenges, or exposed system-prompt UI.',
   'Client exposes prompt-injection attack UX or system prompts — LLM guardrails may be bypassable.',
   'rule_ref',
   '{"rule":"clientSidePromptInjectionEvidence"}'::jsonb,
   'deep',
   '{"summary":"Treat LLM inputs as untrusted; never expose system prompts; rate-limit adversarial probes.","steps":["Remove system-prompt disclosure from client-visible UI and bundles.","Add input/output guardrails and logging for jailbreak attempts.","Rate-limit chat endpoints in production."]}'::jsonb,
   'My app ships prompt-injection red-team UI (adversarial prompts, systemPrompt display). Remove system-prompt leakage from the client and add server-side guardrails on chat inputs.',
   true),
  ('secret-hasura-admin', 'generic', 'Exposed secret', 'critical',
   'Hasura admin secret exposed in client bundle',
   'A Hasura admin secret was found in JavaScript or HTML served to the browser.',
   'A Hasura admin secret bypasses all GraphQL/Postgres authorization rules.',
   'secret_regex',
   '{"regex":"x-hasura-admin-secret[\\"''']?\\\\s*:\\\\s*[\\"'']([A-Za-z0-9]{20,})[\\"'']","secretName":"Hasura admin secret","serverOnly":true}'::jsonb,
   'free',
   '{"summary":"Rotate the Hasura admin secret now and move it server-side.","steps":["Treat the key as compromised and rotate it with the provider immediately.","Remove it from all client code and from any client-exposed env var (e.g. NEXT_PUBLIC_*, VITE_*).","Access the key only from server-side code (route handlers / serverless functions)."]}'::jsonb,
   'A Hasura admin secret is exposed in my client bundle. Remove it from all client-side code and client-exposed environment variables, move every use of it into server-side code, and tell me exactly which files referenced it so I can rotate and confirm.',
   true),
  ('ssrf-endpoint-fetch', 'generic', 'Server-side request forgery', 'high',
   'SSRF — server fetches attacker-controlled URL',
   'An API endpoint accepts a URL parameter and the server fetches it, returning the remote page content in the response. Attackers can use this to reach internal services, cloud metadata, or localhost-only admin panels.',
   'A fetch/proxy endpoint follows arbitrary URLs server-side — internal networks and metadata may be reachable.',
   'rule_ref',
   '{"rule":"ssrfEndpointProbe"}'::jsonb,
   'free',
   '{"summary":"Block SSRF: allow-list destinations, validate resolved IPs, disable redirects.","steps":["Replace open URL fetch with an allow-list of trusted hosts/schemes.","Resolve DNS and reject private, loopback, and link-local IP ranges before connecting.","Disable HTTP redirects on outbound requests and cap response size/timeouts."]}'::jsonb,
   'My API has an SSRF-prone fetch/proxy endpoint that follows user-supplied URLs. Add allow-listing, block private/metadata IPs after DNS resolution, disable redirects, and show the safe server-side fetch handler.',
   true),
  ('pentest-forge-linked-lab-probe', 'generic', 'Information disclosure', 'medium',
   'Public vulnerable lab catalog with linked benchmark targets',
   'Page catalogs PentestForge *.lab.pentest-forge.com vulnerable apps (Juice Shop, crAPI, VAmPI, Tomcat, WebLogic) or a linked subdomain returned unauthenticated vulnerable-app data.',
   'Public benchmark playground exposes live vulnerable targets — scanners and attackers can enumerate OWASP/API/CVE labs.',
   'rule_ref',
   '{"rule":"pentestForgeLinkedLabProbe"}'::jsonb,
   'deep',
   '{"summary":"Restrict lab hubs to authenticated testers; do not expose production-adjacent domains publicly.","steps":["Gate benchmark playgrounds behind auth or VPN.","Use robots/noindex and avoid linking live vulnerable apps from public marketing pages.","Isolate lab subnets from production networks."]}'::jsonb,
   'Our site links to public PentestForge vulnerable lab subdomains. Show how to restrict the catalog to authenticated users and network-isolate benchmark targets.',
   true),
  ('client-side-owasp-educational-lab-evidence', 'generic', 'Injection', 'medium',
   'OWASP Top 10 educational lab pages document injectable patterns',
   'Crawled Docusaurus or static OWASP lab content includes walkthroughs for SQL injection (patient_lookup.php, UNION SELECT), IDOR enumeration, or broken access-control flaws — the tutorial itself documents exploitable patterns.',
   'Public OWASP lab tutorials ship vulnerable code samples attackers can study and replay on real targets.',
   'rule_ref',
   '{"rule":"clientSideOwaspEducationalLabEvidence"}'::jsonb,
   'deep',
   '{"summary":"Host lab tutorials on isolated domains; use sanitized code samples in production docs.","steps":["Keep intentionally vulnerable tutorial code on dedicated lab hosts, not production apps.","Replace live exploit strings in public docs with redacted or parameterized examples.","Gate hands-on labs behind authentication when they include runnable vulnerable snippets."]}'::jsonb,
   'Our OWASP Top 10 lab site publishes SQL injection and IDOR walkthroughs with patient_lookup.php and UNION SELECT examples. Show how to host these on an isolated lab domain and redact exploitable snippets from public documentation.',
   true),
  ('client-side-jwt-none-evidence', 'generic', 'Broken authentication', 'high',
   'Client bundle documents JWT alg:none acceptance',
   'The shipped JavaScript includes a JWT lab where the none algorithm is accepted and role can be escalated to admin — signature verification is bypassable when the server mirrors this logic.',
   'JWT alg:none lets attackers forge admin tokens without a valid signature.',
   'rule_ref',
   '{"rule":"clientSideJwtNoneEvidence"}'::jsonb,
   'deep',
   '{"summary":"Reject alg:none; enforce HMAC/RSA signature verification server-side.","steps":["Maintain an allowlist of permitted JWT algorithms (e.g. RS256, HS256).","Reject tokens with alg:none or missing signatures before parsing claims.","Remove JWT attack lab code from production bundles."]}'::jsonb,
   'My app accepts JWT alg:none and allows role escalation to admin. Show server-side middleware that rejects unsigned tokens, enforces RS256/HS256 only, and validates role claims after signature verification.',
   true),
  ('client-side-xss-c2-collector-evidence', 'generic', 'Cross-site scripting', 'high',
   'XSS C2 collector dashboard with unauthenticated /api/collect exfil endpoint',
   'The page documents an attacker C2 dashboard for XSS cookie theft, including /api/collect and cross-origin img onerror exfil techniques. GET /api/collect may respond without auth.',
   'Public XSS collector endpoints let any site exfiltrate victim session data to an attacker-controlled dashboard.',
   'rule_ref',
   '{"rule":"clientSideXssC2CollectorEvidence"}'::jsonb,
   'deep',
   '{"summary":"Remove public C2 collectors; enforce HttpOnly cookies and strict CSP.","steps":["Do not deploy XSS exfil collector APIs on production domains.","Set HttpOnly and Secure on session cookies so document.cookie cannot read them.","Use a strict Content-Security-Policy to block inline script injection."]}'::jsonb,
   'Our app hosts an XSS C2 collector at /api/collect that receives stolen cookies cross-origin. Show how to remove the collector, set HttpOnly session cookies, and add CSP to block cookie theft via XSS.',
   true),
  ('client-side-devsecops-lab-evidence', 'generic', 'Broken access control', 'high',
   'DevSecOps microservices lab documents IDOR and gateway bypass attacks',
   'The client bundle catalogs DevSecOps Hacking Lab attack scenarios — IDOR profile access, gateway bypass, brute force, MFA bypass, plus SIEM/WAF monitoring modules.',
   'Educational attack consoles on public URLs teach adversaries reusable IDOR and auth-bypass patterns against real APIs.',
   'rule_ref',
