   'deep',
   '{"summary":"Keep Chimera honeypot docs and deployments on isolated lab networks.","steps":["Do not expose Chimera vuln-api instances to the public internet without WAF protection.","Gate vulnerability inventory pages behind authentication for internal red-team use only.","Segment honeypot subnets from production VPCs."]}'::jsonb,
   'Our site documents the Chimera vuln-api honeypot with CHM-ID vulnerability inventory. Show how to restrict docs to internal red-team networks and isolate honeypot deployments.',
   true),
  ('client-side-hack-health-lab-evidence', 'generic', 'Injection', 'high',
   'Hack Health tutorial documents intentional SQL injection lab',
   'Nextra tutorial pages walk through CWE-89 SQL injection on the HackHealth login — string-concatenated queries and UNION SELECT pg_user enumeration.',
   'Educational SQLi walkthrough on a public deploy teaches reusable PostgreSQL injection patterns against the live login API.',
   'rule_ref',
   '{"rule":"clientSideHackHealthLabEvidence"}'::jsonb,
   'deep',
   '{"summary":"Use parameterized queries and restrict tutorial labs to local dev.","steps":["Replace string-concatenated SQL with parameterized queries or an ORM.","Host HackHealth attack tutorials on localhost only, not public Vercel deploys.","Remove UNION-based enumeration examples from production-facing docs."]}'::jsonb,
   'Our HackHealth tutorial documents intentional SQL injection with UNION SELECT against pg_user. Show parameterized query fixes and how to gate the attack lab behind local-only access.',
   true),
  ('openapi-debug-password-exposure', 'generic', 'Sensitive data exposure', 'critical',
   'OpenAPI debug endpoint exposes cleartext passwords',
